From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: karsyboy <karsyboy@k-ops.cloud>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:32:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] decoder: validate coefficient packets before upload

A packet's header announces how many payload words follow, but the GPU
unpacker trusts the plane counts and significance bits inside them. A
malformed or truncated packet from the network could make it read past
the payload. Validate every byte the unpacker consumes with byte loads
before a packet is queued, reject a sequence header announcing more
blocks than the frame holds, and copy headers instead of dereferencing
possibly unaligned packet memory.

The bitstream structures move to pyrowave_bitstream.hpp so validation
and tests can use them without Granite.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
